--- AttachEvidence on AUTH-HAPPY-1 (as OEM) -- FIRST ATTEMPT, AFTER DELIVERY ---
Error: endorsement failure during invoke. response: status:500 message:"attachEvidence rejected: caller Org1MSP is not the current owner of token AUTH-HAPPY-1 (owner is Dealer1)"

*** GENUINE FINDING, NOT A SCRIPTED NEGATIVE CASE: this call was intended
*** as part of the authorised happy path but was rejected. RecordDelivery
*** (the immediately preceding step) sets Owner to a caller-supplied dealer
*** label ("Dealer1"), which is not a real MSP identity on this
*** three-organisation network (OEM, Tier-1 supplier, Regulator only). No
*** enrolled identity can ever equal "Dealer1", so requireCallerIsOwner
*** rejects every caller, authorised or not, once a token has been
*** delivered. This is recorded here exactly as it happened and is treated
*** as an additional, real limitation of this design (see Limitations),
*** not silently corrected out of the evidence trail. The script was fixed
*** to call AttachEvidence before RecordDelivery, and the corrected
*** ordering is confirmed working further below.

